<title>CHINA: China cotton output 4.0 mln tonnes in 1996.</title>
<headline>China cotton output 4.0 mln tonnes in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's output of cotton in 1996 was estimated at 4.0 million tonnes, down by 800,000 tonnes from last year, the State Statistical Bureau said.  </p>
<p>Earlier estimates had placed the cotton crop for 1995 at about 4.4 million tonnes and it was unclear if that figure had been revised.</p>
<p>The bureau estimated a record grain harvest of 480 million tonnes for 1996, up from a previous record of 466 million tonnes last year.</p>
<p>It estimated total production of oil-bearing crops at 21.9 million tonnes, falling by about 600,000 tonnes from last year.</p>
</text>
